    "q": "Given that $z = -\\sqrt{3} + i$, find $z^6$. Give your answer in the form $x + yi$, where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution:</strong><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z = -\\sqrt{3} + i = (-\\sqrt{3},\\ 1)$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$r = \\sqrt{3 + 1} = 2$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$\\cos\\theta = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\quad \\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$\\theta = \\frac{5\\pi}{6}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z = 2\\left(\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}{6} + i\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\right)$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z^6 = 2^6\\left(\\cos 5\\pi + i\\sin 5\\pi\\right)$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z^6 = 64(-1 + 0i) = -64$</div><br><br><strong>Final Answer: $-64 + 0i$</strong>"
