    "q": "Find the value of $z^5$ where $z = -1 - i$. Give your answer in the form $x + yi$.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution:</strong><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z = -1 - i = (-1,\\ -1)$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$r = \\sqrt{1 + 1} = \\sqrt{2}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$\\cos\\theta = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\quad \\sin\\theta = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$\\theta = -\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z = \\sqrt{2}\\left(\\cos\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right) + i\\sin\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right)$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z^5 = (\\sqrt{2})^5\\left(\\cos\\left(-\\frac{15\\pi}{4}\\right) + i\\sin\\left(-\\frac{15\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right)$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$-\\frac{15\\pi}{4} + 4\\pi = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z^5 = 4\\sqrt{2}\\left(\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{4} + i\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 4 + 4i$</div><br><br><strong>Final Answer: $4 + 4i$</strong>"
  },
