    "q": "Let $z = 3 + 2i$. Find $\\frac{z}{\\bar{z}}$ in the form $x + yi$.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution:</strong><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$\\bar{z} = 3 - 2i$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$\\frac{z}{\\bar{z}} = \\frac{3 + 2i}{3 - 2i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 2i}{3 + 2i}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$= \\frac{(3 + 2i)^2}{9 + 4} = \\frac{9 + 12i + 4i^2}{13}$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$= \\frac{5 + 12i}{13} = \\frac{5}{13} + \\frac{12}{13}i$</div><br><br><strong>Final Answer: $\\frac{5}{13} + \\frac{12}{13}i$</strong>"
  },
