    "q": "Find the complex number $z$ such that $z + 3\\bar{z} = 4 + 2i$.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution:</strong><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>Let $z = x + yi$, then $\\bar{z} = x - yi$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$(x + yi) + 3(x - yi) = 4 + 2i$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$4x - 2yi = 4 + 2i$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$4x = 4 \\implies x = 1$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$-2y = 2 \\implies y = -1$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z = 1 - i$</div><br><br><strong>Final Answer: $1 - i$</strong>"
