    "c": "<strong>Solution:</strong><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>If $z = r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)$, then $z^{-1} = \\frac{1}{r}\\left(\\cos(-\\theta)+i\\sin(-\\theta)\\right)$</div><br><br><div style='overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 8px;'>$z^{-1} = \\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{3} + i\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\right)$</div><br><br><strong>Final Answer: $\\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{3} + i\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\right]$</strong>"
